    <!-- Tutorial script -->
    <string name="pt_tut_01">Welcome to the archipelago. Buy tiles, collect rent, and outlast your rivals.</string>
    <string name="pt_tut_02">Roll two dice and your token sails that many tiles around the ring.</string>
    <string name="pt_tut_03">Land on an unowned tile and you may buy it. Pearls are play money only.</string>
    <string name="pt_tut_04">Land on a rival tile and you pay rent. Own a whole colour and its rent doubles.</string>
    <string name="pt_tut_05">With a whole colour you can build cabins. Build evenly across the colour.</string>
    <string name="pt_tut_06">Four cabins can become a resort, the biggest rent of all.</string>
    <string name="pt_tut_07">Doubles let you roll again. Three doubles in a row sweep you to the Sandbar.</string>
    <string name="pt_tut_08">In the Sandbar, roll doubles, pay the fine or use a free-pass card to leave.</string>
    <string name="pt_tut_09">Tide and Guild cards bring surprises: gifts, bills and sudden moves.</string>
    <string name="pt_tut_10">Short of pearls? Sell buildings or pledge tiles. Pledged tiles collect no rent.</string>
    <string name="pt_tut_11">If you cannot pay your debt, you go bankrupt and your tiles pass to who you owe.</string>
    <string name="pt_tut_12">The last player standing wins. Quick games end after 20 rounds: richest wins.</string>
    <!-- Coach card and tips -->
    <string name="coach_property_tycoon_s1">Roll two dice and move your token around the ring of 40 tiles.</string>
    <string name="coach_property_tycoon_s2">Buy the tiles you land on, or send them to auction so a rival pays more.</string>
    <string name="coach_property_tycoon_s3">Own every tile of one colour to double its rent and start building cabins.</string>
    <string name="coach_property_tycoon_s4">Pledge tiles or sell buildings if you owe more pearls than you hold.</string>
    <string name="coach_property_tycoon_s5">Be the last player standing, or the richest when the round limit arrives.</string>
    <string name="coach_property_tycoon_fact">Games like this began a century ago as a protest board that taught how rent can pile up in few hands.</string>
    <string name="draft_tip_property_tycoon_1">Whole colours matter more than single tiles. Trade toward a set.</string>
    <string name="draft_tip_property_tycoon_2">Keep a cash cushion. One resort rent can end your game.</string>
    <string name="draft_tip_property_tycoon_3">Three cabins is the sweet spot: the rent jumps most for the price.</string>
